PATCH 562: the player's joystick-device controller 0000:a57a and the drive-state cluster it switches on
(a376 a3a8 a3e2 a5b0 a5cd a5f1) -- base loss, dropped dispatch arity, and mis-widened WORD fields.

a57a is called once per tick by all four type-A update templates (7c1d/87df/902c/97d5, `call 0xa57a`
right after the fire step) and acts only on the player's object (`cmp 0x6d34,%di`).  While no manual
routine is engaged (`testw $1,0x40(%di)`) it runs the per-device tick selected by word[DGROUP:0x8b43]
through the table at 0x976c, then the input sub-state byte[di+0xa0] through the table at 0x9778.
word[0x8b43] is the SETTINGS screen's CONTROL field -- NO JOYSTICK / STD JOYSTICK / FLIGHTSTICK
W-THROTTLE / THRUSTMASTER FCS / CH FLIGHTSTICK PRO / THRUSTMASTER WCS / EXTERNAL DRIVER, 0..6 -- and the
0x976c entries are a5ea a5eb a5f1 a62a a624 a630 a59b in that order (the settings string builder 6f90,
patch 559, prints it as its first digit).  The port had every one of these dead:

  * the callers passed the HOST pointer, so a57a's `param_1 == DAT_2000_2d34` (host pointer vs the near
    offset 0xc05c) was never true and the whole controller was a silent no-op -- no crash to flag it;
  * inside, `[di+0x40]` / `[di+0xa0]` were host derefs and both table lookups bare host addresses;
  * both dispatches passed NO argument to targets that read DI (the 556-class arity defect);
  * a376/a3a8 (turn), a3e2 (heading step), a5b0/a5cd (gun elevation), a5f1 (flightstick tick) all
    host-deref'd DI, read their rate/far tables at bare addresses, and widened the WORD fields [di+0x8b]
    (heading), [di+0x30], [di+0x38] (elevation, SIGNED clamps 0x238c / -0x1554) to 4-byte ints -- the
    same width class as patches 547-553;
  * a5f1's `lcall *0x971e(%bx)` is a FAR-pointer table (type*4; type 0 -> 0f69:7fe1 = FUN_1000_7671)
    that Ghidra turned into a near icall with 0xf69 passed as an ARGUMENT.

Convention: DI is threaded positionally into the target's param_1 (patch 455 for a3ec, 543 for
a3f6/a432 -- the already-correct members of this same cluster).  aae8's AX pass-through is dead on every
path: its per-type takeover table at 0x995a has entries only for types 0..3 (784d 7faf 8cc8 9407) and
none reads AX (784d is `movb $3,0xc7(%di); ret`), so `aae8(di, di)` / `aae8(0, di)` are exact.

Not a self-play change: with empty input and the default device 0 the 0x976c entry is a5ea = `ret` and
[di+0xa0] stays 0 -> a59b = `ret`, so nothing here moves an AI-vs-AI run.  It IS the player's control
path -- every joystick mode named on the SETTINGS screen ran through a dead function.

What this cluster is NOT: it is not "AUTO CONTROL".  The HUD's AUTO CONTROL label is the SETTINGS
screen's separate AUTO TURRET CONTROL checkbox (byte[di+0x3f]&8, toggled by the cockpit click handlers
at 0x74b9..0x8471), i.e. turret auto-aim.  No code path drives the player's hull without input; [di+0x38]
is the GUN ELEVATION (a202 nudges it on the elevation keys, a2a8 zeroes it on target loss, a265 writes
a18e's pitch into it), and the hull speed is word[di+0x57] (a410..a431).

